    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "BARRY AUCTIONEERS & VALUERS are delighted to welcome you to this charming four-bedroom semi-detached home, ideally situated in the established and sought-after Endsleigh Estate on Douglas Road.\r\nBuilt approximately 60 years ago, this is a property that has stood the test of time and has been well maintained and cared for throughout the years. It offers approximately 130 square metres of accommodation, providing generous living space for families, couples, or anyone looking for a substantial home in a mature residential setting.\r\nAs you enter, the property immediately gives a sense of the space and character that you would expect from a home of this era. The accommodation is well proportioned, with excellent potential for modern family living while retaining many of the features and proportions associated with older houses.\r\nThe four bedrooms provide flexibility for a growing family, home office, guest accommodation, or additional living space depending on the purchaser's needs.\r\nThe property's approximately 130 square metres of floor area gives it a very practical layout, with good separation between the living and sleeping accommodation.\r\nOne of the key attractions is the location. Endsleigh Estate is an established residential development on Douglas Road, offering the benefits of a mature neighbourhood while being conveniently positioned for access to local amenities, schools, transport links and the wider Cork area.\r\nImportantly, this is a home that has been well looked after for its age. While prospective purchasers will naturally appreciate that the property dates from around 60 years ago, it has been maintained over the years and presents an opportunity to acquire a substantial home with plenty of scope for a new owner to make it their own.\r\nFor buyers looking for a property with space, established surroundings and genuine long-term potential, this four-bedroom semi-detached house is certainly one to consider.\r\nIn summary, we have approximately 130 square metres, four bedrooms, a mature and well-established location, and a property that has been carefully maintained throughout its life. It offers both comfortable accommodation today and the opportunity for the next owner to update or enhance it according to their own taste and requirements.\r\nWe'd be delighted to welcome you to view the property and appreciate the space and potential it offers."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Accommodation\r\nPorch: \r\nSliding doors lead to the entrance porch.\r\n\r\nEntrance Hallway:    \r\nA timber front door with glass insert panelling leads to the hallway that has timber flooring. There is storage under the stairs. \r\n\r\nLiving room:  4.5m x 3.6m\r\nThis room has one large window overlooking the front with curtain pole and curtains, carpet flooring, one centre light. \r\nGlass double doors to:\r\nLounge : 4.2m x 4.0m\r\nThis room has French doors leading to patio area with curtains pole, curtains and carpet flooring, one centre light, feature  fireplace. \r\n\r\nKitchen : 4.7m x 3.01m\r\nThe kitchen has tiled floor, fitted units and stainless steel sink & drainer. There are two windows overlooking rear garden. \r\nUtility room : Power points and plumbed for a washer and dryer. \r\nGuest wc : \r\nWC & window to rear \r\nGarage:  5.1m x 2.9m\r\nThere is access from the side and one roller door. The gas bouler is located here. \r\nUpstairs:\r\nBedroom1: 4.0m x 3.7m\r\nThis room has one window overlooking the front with curtain pole and curtains, carpet flooring and one centre light. \r\n\r\nBedroom 2:   4.0m x 3.1m\r\nThis room has one window overlooking the rear with blind, carpet flooring and one centre light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3:   3.7m x 3.5m\r\nThis room has one window overlooking the rear with curtain pole and curtains, carpet flooring and one centre light.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4:  3.1m x 2.6m\r\nThis room has one window overlooking the front with curtain pole and curtains, carpet flooring and one centre light.\r\nBathroom:  Modern three-piece bathroom suite incorporating standalone shower unit with electric shower, wash hand basin and wc. There is one frosted window overlooking the rear, tiled flooring and walls, one centre light and a heated towel rack and mirror. \r\nOutside:\r\nThe rear garden is west facing ideal for summer barbeques.\r\nThis side and front garden have mature shrubs and trees and has off street parking."
      },
